Validation - first code review after checkpoint 12
==================================================

Run these checks from the repository as `codexuser`. Review every destructive
or live-provider command before execution.

1. Unit and database integration tests
--------------------------------------

    UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/webcam-uv-cache uv run pytest -q \
      tests/ingestion tests/worker tests/metrics tests/notification tests/storage

Apply migrations through the Compose gate and run the database tests:

    docker compose --env-file .env run --rm schema-migrate
    RUN_DATABASE_TESTS=1 UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/webcam-uv-cache \
      uv run --env-file .env pytest -q tests/database

Confirm `source_stream` contains only these five ingestion-state columns:
`last_observed_provider_timestamp`, `last_observed_image_marker`,
`last_download_timestamp`, `last_processed_timestamp`, and
`estimated_source_stream_period`. Confirm `publication_outbox` no longer exists.

2. Container build and bounded jobs
-----------------------------------

    docker compose --env-file .env --profile application --profile monitoring \
      --profile jobs config --quiet
    docker compose --env-file .env build webcam-job windy-worker \
      fintraffic-worker skaping-worker

Run bounded or dry-run discovery and ingestion before enabling continuous
workers. Confirm secrets are not printed.

3. Freshness and retry state
----------------------------

For one stream per network, inspect observed timestamp/marker, processed
timestamp, EMA, and last download-decision time. Confirm:

- unchanged available indicators skip the pipeline;
- a changed provider timestamp updates cadence estimation only after a
  download is selected;
- an observation excluded by scheduling changes no database state;
- a failed later stage does not advance processed state;
- a later due pass retries that observed image;
- Fintraffic and Skaping unchanged ETags avoid repeated processing;
- Skaping MQTT source-image metadata contains only a sanitized resolved path.

4. Delivery observability
-------------------------

Cause one controlled retry in fixture tests or a non-production environment.
Confirm each retry increments `webcam_image_retry_total`, while
`webcam_s3_upload_total` or `webcam_mqtt_publication_total` increments exactly
once with the final success or failure.

Confirm worker dashboards show five-minute S3 and MQTT operation counts and no
publication-outbox panel.

5. Cleanup safety
-----------------

    just container-cleanup-spool 24 --dry-run --limit 10 --show-keys
    just container-cleanup-spool 24 --dry-run \
      --all-transformation-prefixes --limit 10 --show-keys

Confirm the first command selects only T0 and the second still ignores
unknown and database-backup keys.

After a verified backup exists, inspect conservative backup cleanup:

    just container-cleanup-database-backups \
      backups/postgresql/YYYY/MM/DD/webcam_ingestion_YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ.dump \
      --dry-run --show-keys

Confirm only the latest preceding available day in the same month is selected.

6. Compose and systemd handoff
------------------------------

Install the reviewed files from `deployment/systemd/pilot/` under
`/etc/systemd/system` with the intended `/opt/webcam-ingestion` deployment
path. Enable `webcam-stack.service`, `webcam-discovery.timer`, and
`webcam-maintenance.timer`.

Confirm Compose owns the three continuously running worker containers and
their restart policies. Confirm systemd schedules sequential discovery at
12:00 UTC and backup followed by cleanup at 01:00 UTC. Check graceful stop,
container restart, persistent database state, worker health, metrics, and
separate logs before beginning checkpoint 13 drills.
